From eb3b6c7bfdc3720ae5329f9d3336bbb9576a4c33 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Francesco Riosa <me@francesco-riosa.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 01:55:35 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] fix(builtins): assignment-expand declaration operands with an
 expanded name

brush's parser only recognises an assignment word when the name is a
literal identifier, so `export ${var}=value` arrived at the builtin as
CommandArg::String. export's String branch then only marked an existing
variable exported (a silent no-op), while declare/local/readonly
reported 'not a valid variable name'. bash assigns after expansion for
declaration builtins (POSIX XCU 2.9.1).

Re-examine the already-expanded string inside the builtins (the small
half of the choice): split on the first `=`, honour `+=`, and route a
valid scalar name through the existing CommandArg::Assignment path, so
scoping, attributes and append semantics are unchanged. A name that is
not a valid identifier produces the diagnostic (export now reports
'invalid identifier' with status 1 instead of succeeding silently);
operands without `=` and compound array values keep their existing
handling. Shared helper in brush-builtins/src/declaration.rs with unit
tests, used by export.rs and declare.rs (which also covers local,
readonly and typeset).

Upstream #1280 reworks this wholesale (centralized word+subscript
passes, declare split, breaking API changes) and is still a Draft; this
lands entirely inside the builtins so it rebases onto #1280 as a
deletion rather than a conflict. Fixes portuale backlog #94 (toolchain-
funcs _tc-getPROG tc-getCC echoing empty under --shell brush).

Developed on branch fix/declaration-assignment-expansion as slice
commits dd016ba6 (fix) + 38447d84 (compat cases); squashed here to the
house one-commit-per-fix shape.

Compat coverage: new declaration-assignment-expansion.yaml over the
matrix (literal | ${var} | "${var}" | append | no-value x export |
declare | local | readonly | typeset), plus 13 previously-known
failures unmarked (quoted scalar/append declare forms, command
declare/export forwarding, the non-reexpanding generated export, the
array-element export rejection).

Verified: brush-compat-tests 2576 ran / 2120 succeeded / 0 unexpected
failures (pre-fix baseline 2568 / 2099 / 0); fmt, clippy and
brush-builtins unit tests clean.

Assisted-by: opencode:muse-spark
